WEBVTT

00:24.405 --> 00:26.657
Man, I'm starving.

00:26.783 --> 00:30.745
After we visit Bro's grave,
let's get something to eat, Josuke.

00:31.037 --> 00:32.788
Eh, I'm not hungry.

00:34.832 --> 00:39.127
ITALIAN CUISINE
TRENDY
100 METERS TO THE LEFT

00:35.458 --> 00:39.086
There's a new Italian restaurant.
Looks like it's just up the road.

00:39.212 --> 00:43.712
ITALIAN CUISINE

00:39.295 --> 00:41.088
Just up the road is the cemetery.

00:41.297 --> 00:44.258
Doesn't seem like
the best location for a new restaurant.

00:44.425 --> 00:45.072
Josuke, it's foodie destinations
like that that bring people in!

00:49.806 --> 00:52.809
"This is to die for!
My mouth can't stop watering!"

00:53.100 --> 00:55.852
I'm sure that's what people say!

00:56.020 --> 00:57.896
Let's go! Come on!

00:59.607 --> 01:00.399
This is it?

01:00.608 --> 01:03.027
TRENDY

01:01.025 --> 01:02.818
I thought this was
a vacant building…

01:03.069 --> 01:06.155
Maybe they remodeled.
It's got character!

01:08.866 --> 01:11.661
What? "Diner dependent"?

01:08.950 --> 01:12.578
TODAY'S MENU
DINER DEPENDENT
WITH COFFEE & DESSERT
3,500 YEN—

01:18.960 --> 01:21.587
Great atmosphere inside, too!

01:22.255 --> 01:23.756
Welcome.

01:24.423 --> 01:28.760
EPISODE 10
LET'S GO EAT SOME ITALIAN FOOD

01:29.136 --> 01:30.345
Two today?

01:30.555 --> 01:32.598
Please, have a seat.

01:32.849 --> 01:34.892
Uh… Thanks…

01:37.979 --> 01:38.854
Please.

01:38.980 --> 01:40.606
R-Right…

01:40.940 --> 01:43.359
Um, are you a foreigner?

01:43.651 --> 01:46.612
Si, Signore. I'm from Italy.

01:47.154 --> 01:50.031
I'm Tonio Trendy.
Call me Tonio.

01:50.116 --> 01:54.616
Yay, this is great!
I get to eat real Italian food!

01:54.704 --> 01:57.248
I traveled to many countries,

01:57.957 --> 01:59.959
and incorporated the best of
the world's culinary traditions

02:00.167 --> 02:02.586
with the flavors of my homeland.

02:03.212 --> 02:06.548
Then I came to Japan
looking for new opportunities.

02:07.091 --> 02:09.551
Morioh is a wonderful town.

02:10.177 --> 02:13.013
You can find many farms
with many kinds of fresh produce.

02:13.222 --> 02:15.265
Its "treasures of the sea"
are wonderful, too.

02:15.641 --> 02:16.725
I like it here very much.

02:17.143 --> 02:19.311
Using Morioh's wonderful ingredients,

02:19.437 --> 02:23.357
I will make you gentlemen
a meal to delight your senses.

02:23.441 --> 02:25.985
All right!
Now what should I get?

02:26.277 --> 02:28.195
Show us the menu immediately!

02:28.571 --> 02:29.446
Menu?

02:30.656 --> 02:32.908
We have no such thing here.

02:34.493 --> 02:38.163
What do you mean
you don't have a menu?

02:38.831 --> 02:41.041
What I serve depends on
who is dining.

02:41.125 --> 02:43.961
So show me the menu!

02:44.045 --> 02:48.545
No, no! I examine my customer,
and then decide what to prepare.

02:49.091 --> 02:50.425
What're you talking about?

02:50.551 --> 02:53.595
So you don't let your customers
eat what they want?

02:56.182 --> 02:59.059
Yesterday, you suffered
a bout of diarrhea, no?

03:01.187 --> 03:02.938
Your intestinal walls are inflamed.

03:03.397 --> 03:05.107
And you're sleep deprived.

03:05.274 --> 03:07.818
You got in only four hours,
am I right?

03:08.361 --> 03:10.029
That explains your puffy eyes.

03:11.238 --> 03:12.948
Now let's see your left hand.

03:14.158 --> 03:14.950
Uh-huh…

03:15.242 --> 03:16.952
Your right foot is infected
with athlete's foot.

03:17.411 --> 03:20.288
You also have two cavities,
and your left shoulder is stiff, right?

03:20.373 --> 03:22.750
H-How do you know all that?!

03:23.042 --> 03:25.044
Everything you said was spot on!

03:25.336 --> 03:29.298
Your hands tell me everything
about your physical condition.

03:30.591 --> 03:32.217
Oh, please excuse me!

03:34.762 --> 03:36.388
And you, Signore?

03:36.889 --> 03:39.850
Yeah, I'm not very hungry.

03:40.434 --> 03:41.685
Just coffee'll be fine.

03:42.144 --> 03:43.061
Make it a cappuccino.

03:43.771 --> 03:44.980
Ho capito.

03:47.525 --> 03:51.779
You do know, super healthy food
usually tastes like crap.

03:52.613 --> 03:55.240
If it tastes even a little gross,
we don't have to pay.

03:55.324 --> 03:56.658
We can complain and leave.

03:56.742 --> 03:57.534
Right.

04:00.204 --> 04:02.080
J-Josuke…

04:02.665 --> 04:06.001
This water…
Or this mineral water…

04:06.127 --> 04:06.836
What's wrong?

04:06.919 --> 04:11.419
I-I've never in my
entire life had water this good!

04:16.595 --> 04:20.181
It's like… it's brimming with elegance.

04:20.891 --> 04:25.228
It's like something a princess in the Alps
playing a harp would drink.

04:25.354 --> 04:27.397
It's gloriously fresh and smooth!

04:27.481 --> 04:31.485
Like that first taste of water after
wandering in the desert for three days!

04:33.404 --> 04:36.115
Y-You aren't kidding!
It's amazing!

04:40.661 --> 04:42.454
Superb!

04:42.747 --> 04:44.457
You're right, it is superb.

04:44.749 --> 04:46.751
What brand of water is this?

04:47.585 --> 04:52.085
I-It's so amazing
I think I'm gonna cry.

04:52.965 --> 04:57.052
Come on, a little sip
of water isn't worth weeping over.

04:57.386 --> 04:59.262
It must be its purity.

04:59.346 --> 05:03.516
Do you have a handkerchief?
The tears are gushing.

05:06.854 --> 05:09.731
They just keep coming!
They won't stop!

05:10.483 --> 05:12.693
O-Okuyasu!
Hey, you're acting weird.

05:13.194 --> 05:14.028
Are you okay?

05:16.280 --> 05:17.030
O-Okuyasu!

05:17.907 --> 05:20.492
Wh-What is with these tears?!

05:20.576 --> 05:22.578
They keep pouring out of me!

05:22.661 --> 05:27.123
Okuyasu, y-your eyes, the eyeball,
the white part…

05:27.208 --> 05:29.793
It's all shriveled and loose!

05:29.919 --> 05:33.589
Momento! Please be calm.

05:34.215 --> 05:37.551
Y-You bastard!
What did you give Okuyasu to drink?

05:37.885 --> 05:41.930
Please calm yourselves.
His eyes are only temporarily withered.

05:42.306 --> 05:45.767
That mineral water is
50,000-year old melted snow

05:45.976 --> 05:48.269
from Mount Kilimanjaro in Africa.

05:48.562 --> 05:51.314
It flushes the eye's interior
of contaminants,

05:51.649 --> 05:54.777
and is an effective
treatment for sleep deprivation.

05:55.528 --> 05:58.197
The reason you didn't cry
from drinking the water is

05:58.280 --> 06:01.574
because you obtained
adequate sleep last night.

06:02.159 --> 06:03.243
Josuke!

06:03.494 --> 06:05.496
My sleepiness is completely gone!

06:05.579 --> 06:10.079
I feel flawless!
Like I slept a full ten hours!

06:10.584 --> 06:11.585
Are you serious?

06:12.086 --> 06:15.506
O-Okuyasu, you sure there's
nothing wrong with your eyes?

06:15.589 --> 06:20.089
Josuke, when you drink water
this good for the first time,

06:20.761 --> 06:23.513
the tears will flow.

06:23.764 --> 06:28.264
I cried more when I watched
<i>Champ</i> on video.

06:28.853 --> 06:30.062
Is that so?

06:30.396 --> 06:31.647
Yes!

06:34.275 --> 06:35.526
Your cappuccino.

06:35.818 --> 06:36.860
R-Right…

06:37.945 --> 06:40.322
Shall we continue
with the next course?

06:42.074 --> 06:44.326
Ooh, this looks good!

06:44.285 --> 06:46.620
INGREDIENTS
• MOZZARELLA CHEESE
(4 PIECES, THINLY SLICED)
• TOMATO (5 PIECES, THINLY SLICED)

06:44.702 --> 06:48.831
For our antipasto,
we have insalata Caprese.

06:46.704 --> 06:49.039
TONIO'S SPECIAL HOUSE DRESSING
• 1 ANCHOVY FILLET • WAKAME
• OLIVE OIL • WHITE WINE VINEGAR
• LEMON JUICE • SALT • PEPPER
• BASIL (ON TOP) • TOASTED BREAD
• LETTUCE (FOR GARNISH)
(SERVE IMMEDIATELY)

06:49.039 --> 06:51.207
M-M-Mozzaza?

06:51.500 --> 06:56.000
Mozzarella is a soft, fresh,
low-fat cheese.

06:57.339 --> 06:59.758
It's a national favorite in Italy.

07:00.009 --> 07:03.971
The first people to use tomatoes as
a culinary ingredient were the Italians.

07:04.054 --> 07:07.891
The Italian people are the world's
leaders of tomato-based cuisine.

07:08.767 --> 07:12.228
That is not bravado.
That is pride.

07:13.480 --> 07:15.690
Please, enjoy.

07:15.983 --> 07:17.317
If you say so!

07:29.747 --> 07:32.374
Well, I guess it is pretty good.

07:33.083 --> 07:35.543
It's good. Very good.

07:36.170 --> 07:40.670
But… I'm not sure what it is,
this cheese doesn't taste like much.

07:42.051 --> 07:42.926
No! No!

07:43.344 --> 07:46.555
You eat it together with the tomato.

07:46.931 --> 07:49.725
What? <i>With</i> the tomato?

07:49.934 --> 07:54.434
Well, most foreign food is incompatible
with Japanese tastes.

07:59.693 --> 08:01.403
My god!

08:02.071 --> 08:02.821
Huh?!

08:04.114 --> 08:08.284
The tomatoey nectar caresses
the fresh, delicate cheese!

08:08.744 --> 08:12.080
The cheese accentuates the tomato,
and the tomato enriches the cheese!

08:12.331 --> 08:16.293
It's a symphony, a harmony of flavors!

08:16.377 --> 08:19.296
It's like Simon and Garfunkel!

08:19.380 --> 08:21.048
Or Ucchan and Nanchan!

08:21.382 --> 08:23.384
It's like the writer-illustrator duo

08:23.467 --> 08:26.761
Asao Takamori and Tetsuya Chiba
from <i>Ashita no Joe!</i>

08:27.096 --> 08:27.971
Grazie!

08:28.305 --> 08:31.099
Nothing makes me happier
than knowing you enjoyed it.

08:31.225 --> 08:34.853
H-Hey, Okuyasu.
Let me have some.

08:34.937 --> 08:36.021
No way.

08:36.480 --> 08:38.940
Order your own!

08:39.275 --> 08:40.985
You're not getting any of this!

08:41.402 --> 08:45.406
I wouldn't give you a piece even
if you were starving to death.

08:53.372 --> 08:55.582
Yuuumy!

08:55.833 --> 08:58.669
Thank you for
giving birth to me, Mom!

08:58.752 --> 09:02.881
Shit! I knew you were
a cheap bastard, but this!

09:03.590 --> 09:06.384
Fine. I'll have one too.

09:07.052 --> 09:08.094
Ho capito.

09:08.929 --> 09:12.849
But the only one getting
his stiff shoulder corrected

09:12.933 --> 09:15.518
is the man with the stiff
shoulder, sitting right there.

09:16.770 --> 09:18.688
Huh? Stiff shoulder?

09:18.939 --> 09:23.276
You know,
my neck does feel kinda hot.

09:23.610 --> 09:25.653
Weird, it's all sweaty.

09:26.280 --> 09:30.617
Signore, may I suggest
you remove your jacket.

09:30.909 --> 09:32.410
I'm getting…

09:34.330 --> 09:36.457
I-I-I'm all itchy!

09:41.587 --> 09:45.966
There's all this flakey stuff
sticking to my fingers!

09:46.216 --> 09:48.676
That is dead skin.

09:48.761 --> 09:49.762
Dead skin?!

09:50.346 --> 09:54.558
It's proof your metabolic
function and circulation has improved.

09:55.017 --> 09:59.517
The calcium, vitamins,
and minerals of the antipasto

10:00.856 --> 10:05.356
have stimulated your thyroid
and its metabolic hormone secretion.

10:08.030 --> 10:10.991
The harmful cells are
being expelled as dead skin.

10:11.116 --> 10:15.120
Please keep scratching,
and remove all that dead skin!

10:21.377 --> 10:23.504
Okuyasu, stop scratching!

10:23.587 --> 10:25.672
You've scratched off
a softball's worth of skin!

10:25.881 --> 10:28.133
You're digging into
your shoulder's muscle!

10:28.425 --> 10:32.095
N-No! You're wrong, Josuke!

10:33.639 --> 10:34.640
So supple!

10:35.307 --> 10:37.392
My shoulder is crazy flexible now!

10:37.518 --> 10:40.312
It's so flexible and light,
it's like it's floating!

10:42.106 --> 10:46.568
Look! Look what my shoulders
can do now!

10:46.693 --> 10:49.070
I've never been able to do this!

10:50.489 --> 10:52.782
That stiffness is good and gone!

10:56.412 --> 10:58.789
Now, if you will excuse me
for a moment.

10:59.289 --> 11:02.667
I have to keep an eye on the pasta.

11:08.215 --> 11:12.715
Amazing!
That Chef Tonio is a genius!

11:13.512 --> 11:15.263
<i>N-No…</i>

11:15.472 --> 11:17.474
<i>This is getting freaky!</i>

11:18.058 --> 11:21.352
<i>There's nothing normal
about this guy's cooking!</i>

11:24.022 --> 11:28.026
MORIOH LANDMARK 3
"ITALIAN RESTAURANT TRENDY"
HOW TO GET THERE: 1 MINUTE'S WALK
FROM MAIN STOP OFF POINT OF MORIOH
KUNIMI MOUNTAIN PASS CEMETARY BUS
AN ECCENTRIC RESTAURANT WHERE
THERE IS NO SET MENU,
AND WHERE THE CHEF DECIDES
HIS MENU ON THE BASIS OF
EACH CUSTOMER'S PHYSICAL CONDITION.
SEATING IS LIMITED.
RESERVATIONS ARE RECOMMENDED.

11:28.193 --> 11:30.445
Now, shall we continue
with our meal?

11:31.029 --> 11:32.572
Now for our Primo piatto.

11:33.198 --> 11:34.449
Today is pasta.

11:34.700 --> 11:37.619
Spaghetti alla puttanesca!

11:35.576 --> 11:40.076
INGREDIENTS
• SPAGHETTI • PITTED BLACK OLIVES
• OLIVE OIL • ANCHOVY FILLET
• GARLIC • CHILI FLAKES
• CHERRY TOMATOES
• PARSLEY, SALT, PEPPER
• PARMESAN CHEESE
(SERVE PIPING HOT)

11:37.744 --> 11:39.620
<i>Literally "whore's pasta,"
the name is said to have</i>

11:39.746 --> 11:42.290
<i>originated with prostitutes
who favored the dish's</i>

11:42.541 --> 11:43.917
<i>easy preparation and
uniquely delectable flavors.</i>

11:44.376 --> 11:46.858
<i>Cheese is not usually added to
pasta prepared with garlic,</i>

11:48.046 --> 11:50.298
<i>but this dish is an exception.</i>

11:50.549 --> 11:54.844
Does this spaghetti
have chili flakes in it?

11:54.970 --> 11:56.513
Yes, it does.

11:56.638 --> 12:01.138
ROME
NAPLES
SPAGHETTI TAGLIATELLE LINGUINE
FUSILLI PENNE FARFALLE
LASAGNE CONCHIGLIE TUBETTI

11:56.763 --> 11:58.973
The sauce in Spaghetti Puttanesca is

11:59.057 --> 12:02.268
one of the oldest recipes
of Italian cuisine.

12:03.270 --> 12:07.274
And my hometown, Naples,
is considered its birthplace.

12:07.858 --> 12:09.672
I give it my highest recommendation.

12:11.278 --> 12:15.156
Oh, but… I can't eat spicy things.

12:15.449 --> 12:17.576
The only kind of curry rice
I can handle is

12:17.659 --> 12:20.578
that mild Vermont Curry
that has apples and honey in it.

12:20.913 --> 12:23.123
Wasabi with sushi is no good, either.

12:24.750 --> 12:26.918
I can't! It's too spicy!

12:27.753 --> 12:29.379
This is way too spicy!

12:29.588 --> 12:32.507
If you can't eat spicy food, Okuyasu,

12:32.674 --> 12:34.050
then don't eat it.

12:39.097 --> 12:41.682
If it doesn't please you,
please don't force yourself.

12:41.850 --> 12:44.936
I'm happy to take
the pasta off your bill.

12:45.062 --> 12:49.483
I will now prepare your
main course, the secondo piatto.

12:50.317 --> 12:54.195
But you know sir,
I make my spaghetti to be enjoyed

12:54.321 --> 12:56.656
even by those who cannot
tolerate spicy food.

13:00.410 --> 13:02.578
Being sensitive to spiciness is okay?

13:03.080 --> 13:03.830
Hot!

13:04.164 --> 13:08.042
Look, I know he's a master chef,
that Tonio…

13:08.460 --> 13:11.004
There's no question, he's a genius!

13:11.171 --> 13:13.173
But this wasn't his best work.

13:13.257 --> 13:16.301
No, I think you may've lucked out
with your spice intolerance.

13:18.095 --> 13:21.264
Don't you think this food and
that water are a little too weird?

13:21.390 --> 13:22.432
Something's shady!

13:22.516 --> 13:24.392
Shady? Like what?

13:24.476 --> 13:25.226
Spicy!

13:25.561 --> 13:27.688
You produced a softball-sized wad
of dead skin,

13:27.938 --> 13:30.231
and cried a river back there!

13:30.691 --> 13:31.775
I guess I did…

13:31.900 --> 13:34.694
When I went to Shirabu Onsen
in Yamagata,

13:34.861 --> 13:38.239
I lost even more dead skin,
and my back got better!

13:38.490 --> 13:40.492
That's totally normal.

13:40.659 --> 13:41.284
Hot!

13:41.368 --> 13:45.580
Listen! Remember what
Toshikazu Hazamada said.

13:46.373 --> 13:49.584
<i>For whatever reason,
whether or not they know each other…</i>

13:49.918 --> 13:52.754
Stand users are
inadvertently drawn to each other.

13:52.963 --> 13:53.838
Josuke!

13:53.964 --> 13:56.591
Are you saying Tonio is
a Stand user?

13:56.717 --> 14:00.804
Shh! We don't know for sure yet!
That's why I said "shady"!

14:01.138 --> 14:02.639
Shady, eh?

14:03.724 --> 14:05.934
Hot! No way!

14:06.059 --> 14:09.896
If you don't like spicy food,
quit putting it in your mouth!

14:10.647 --> 14:12.190
You're right.

14:12.774 --> 14:15.777
Spicy food and me don't mix, but…

14:15.944 --> 14:20.281
for some reason,
I can't stop tasting this sauce.

14:25.579 --> 14:27.080
Why are you eating that?!

14:27.205 --> 14:31.292
I-I know!
Usually I can't eat stuff this spicy…

14:31.585 --> 14:32.377
But…

14:34.588 --> 14:38.967
I can't stop. After that first bite,
the spiciness just pulled me in.

14:39.259 --> 14:43.759
It's like eating your age
in beans during Setsubun,

14:44.139 --> 14:47.016
and even though they don't taste good,
before you know it,

14:47.100 --> 14:49.894
you've eaten a whole bag!

14:52.939 --> 14:55.441
Hey, I told you to stop eating!

14:56.526 --> 14:59.946
I'm getting hungrier!

15:00.030 --> 15:03.825
The more I eat,
the more I want to scarf down!

15:03.909 --> 15:06.369
It's so good!

15:06.453 --> 15:08.204
Okuyasu, you…

15:12.834 --> 15:14.669
Your tooth!
You just lost your tooth!

15:14.753 --> 15:18.047
My cavity!
My rotten tooth fell out!

15:25.138 --> 15:28.599
Actually, I think I had
a cavity below, too…

15:30.560 --> 15:33.020
Another rotten tooth!

15:45.492 --> 15:47.827
Your tooth!
A molar is already growing in?!

15:51.998 --> 15:55.543
That's it.
I don't know what he's scheming…

15:56.336 --> 15:57.754
Shining Diamond!

16:03.844 --> 16:05.470
I wanted to eat more…

16:05.721 --> 16:09.808
I'm gonna revert the ingredients
to their original forms!

16:24.906 --> 16:27.033
What were those little things?

16:27.159 --> 16:28.034
A Stand!

16:28.452 --> 16:32.289
So Tonio Trendy is a Stand user,
after all!

16:36.626 --> 16:37.918
Are you okay, Okuyasu?

16:38.420 --> 16:40.463
My sleepiness is gone.

16:40.547 --> 16:42.131
My stiffness melted away,

16:42.215 --> 16:44.258
and my cavities were replaced
with healthy teeth, but…

16:44.718 --> 16:49.218
M-My stomach hurts!
It's excruciating!

16:51.016 --> 16:51.766
Wait!

16:51.975 --> 16:54.227
Tonio! What the hell
are you pulling here?!

17:05.906 --> 17:06.948
<i>Where is he?</i>

17:09.242 --> 17:11.535
<i>So he finished our main course…</i>

17:26.343 --> 17:29.554
Good, good… You enjoy that.

17:29.638 --> 17:34.138
It appears my main dish of lamb
with apple relish was a success.

17:39.356 --> 17:40.106
What?!

17:41.775 --> 17:44.068
And what are you doing there?

17:44.319 --> 17:46.446
So you saw!

17:52.285 --> 17:56.580
So you came in here to spy on me?!

18:00.252 --> 18:03.922
You will pay for this! Get ready!

18:04.172 --> 18:08.672
Why should I have to stand here listening
to you threatening <i>me</i> to pay?

18:08.885 --> 18:09.927
That's my line!

18:10.011 --> 18:13.014
Just what the hell are you trying
to do with that "food" of yours?!

18:15.851 --> 18:16.810
Okuyasu!

18:18.144 --> 18:19.687
What are you eating?!

18:20.063 --> 18:24.025
I can't stand it! My stomach hurts,
but I can't stop eating!

18:24.192 --> 18:25.610
The tangy-sweet apple relish

18:25.777 --> 18:30.277
and juice from the lamb
makes every bite pure ecstasy!

18:30.907 --> 18:34.118
To think food could taste like this!

18:34.578 --> 18:36.580
Drop that meat, Okuyasu!

18:36.872 --> 18:41.372
The joy!
The pleasure keeps on going!

18:42.043 --> 18:44.670
Amazing!

18:47.924 --> 18:50.051
M-My guts…

18:53.763 --> 18:55.848
My stomach!

18:59.102 --> 19:00.645
Okuyasu!

19:04.065 --> 19:06.067
You'll pay for this!

19:06.860 --> 19:08.278
You bastard!

19:09.487 --> 19:12.282
Wash your hands with soap right now!

19:12.032 --> 19:14.909
MEDICATED

19:12.657 --> 19:13.741
Huh?!

19:13.825 --> 19:14.909
It's inexcusable!

19:15.035 --> 19:17.746
Entering a kitchen
without permission is inexcusable!

19:18.079 --> 19:18.829
You!

19:19.122 --> 19:22.125
Cleanliness in the kitchen
is number one!

19:22.584 --> 19:23.793
S-Soap?

19:24.169 --> 19:25.295
You want me to wash my hands?

19:25.503 --> 19:27.087
Hey, Josuke!

19:27.422 --> 19:29.757
My insides feel rejuvenated!

19:30.175 --> 19:31.676
I feel full, too.

19:31.760 --> 19:33.428
I feel totally content.

19:33.511 --> 19:34.053
Huh?!

19:34.137 --> 19:36.848
My poopy tummy's all better!

19:36.932 --> 19:38.266
What?!

19:39.601 --> 19:41.477
Well isn't that magnificent!

19:41.561 --> 19:46.061
Knowing my cooking brought
happiness and health to my customer

19:47.275 --> 19:50.528
gives me no greater joy or happiness.

19:52.364 --> 19:53.281
That puppy…

19:54.240 --> 19:57.576
With such unconventional flavors,
I wanted him to taste it first.

19:57.911 --> 20:01.080
His digestion was off, too.

20:01.331 --> 20:05.831
Y-You… really only wanted
Okuyasu to enjoy a good meal?

20:07.921 --> 20:11.382
What else could a chef want?

20:11.466 --> 20:15.303
It is what I live for.
It is all I hope for.

20:15.679 --> 20:17.389
So you're a Stand user.

20:19.182 --> 20:20.391
We are, too.

20:22.102 --> 20:24.145
Oh, I don't believe it!

20:25.522 --> 20:29.108
When… When I was traveling
the world

20:29.192 --> 20:33.613
searching for the perfect cuisine,
I discovered my powers.

20:34.197 --> 20:37.825
Never before have I met
anyone with similar powers.

20:38.660 --> 20:39.410
But…

20:39.619 --> 20:41.912
You need some common sense!

20:42.080 --> 20:42.830
Huh?

20:42.914 --> 20:45.499
You touched my kitchen without
washing your hands!

20:45.667 --> 20:48.920
A kitchen's worst enemy is germs!

20:49.004 --> 20:50.922
That's why I was angry!

20:51.006 --> 20:54.676
H-Huh? I-I'm sorry!
I wasn't thinking!

20:54.968 --> 20:56.844
You had better be ready!

20:57.429 --> 20:59.764
Now, shall we continue
with the cooking?

21:02.642 --> 21:04.935
Dessert is… pudding?

21:05.770 --> 21:07.521
But I'm a tough guy!

21:07.772 --> 21:10.483
Hmph! What a load of crap.

21:11.651 --> 21:13.694
My god!

21:13.820 --> 21:15.905
You really are a genius!

21:15.989 --> 21:18.783
A chef of your caliber
makes me proud

21:18.867 --> 21:21.870
- to be a resident of Morioh!
- Dammit, Okuyasu!

21:23.121 --> 21:25.540
Should I assume you enjoyed that?

21:27.000 --> 21:29.293
Hey! I don't see any scrubbing!

21:29.377 --> 21:31.170
Miserable…

21:31.254 --> 21:33.547
Hey, my athlete's foot is gone!

21:34.424 --> 21:37.718
I shall await your return. Grazie!

21:40.013 --> 21:44.058
TRENDY

21:45.852 --> 21:48.563
POLE JAM

21:57.030 --> 21:59.490
Jotaro Kujo, I presume?

22:00.075 --> 22:02.035
I'm with the Speedwagon Foundation.

22:04.287 --> 22:07.081
For now, any electrical wiring
poses a threat,

22:07.248 --> 22:09.124
that includes phone lines
and power lines.

22:09.375 --> 22:11.877
That is why I've come
to deliver this message in the flesh.

22:12.629 --> 22:16.591
"I expect to arrive at
the port of Morioh at noon, tomorrow.

22:24.349 --> 22:26.392
—Joseph Joestar."

23:39.382 --> 23:42.510
EPISODE 11
CHILI PEPPER, PART 1
